<title>BELGIUM: Belgian tax receipts up 3.4 pct in March 1997.</title>
<headline>Belgian tax receipts up 3.4 pct in March 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total Belgian fiscal receipts were up 3.4 percent in March from March 1996 and up 4.9 percent in the first three months of 1997 from the same 1996 period, the Finance Ministry said in a statement.  </p>
<p>TAX RECEIPTS (in million bfr)</p>
<p>					 March 97   March 96   pct change</p>
<p>    Total			    150,189    145,299	3.4</p>
<p>    Direct taxation		 78,743     95,716    -17.7</p>
<p>    V.A.T and similar taxes     42,911     41,213	4.1</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE TAX RECEIPTS (in million bfr)</p>
<p>				     Jan-Mar 97  Jan-Mar 96  pct change</p>
<p>    Total			    493,825    470,944	4.9</p>
<p>    Direct taxation		284,676    263,664	8.0</p>
<p>    V.A.T and similar taxes    123,982    121,459	2.1</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
